        "titulo": "Asking for help and for explanations",
        "explicacao": "«Kannst du …?» (informal) and «Können Sie …?» (formal) are the most common ways to ask for something — like \"Can you…?\" / \"Could you…?\". The main verb goes to the END, in the infinitive. Learn these classroom phrases: they work in any conversation with a German speaker and already show up in A1 exams. «langsamer» means \"more slowly\" — the -er works like English -er.",
